WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.160
Good morning Hank, it’s Tuesday.

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.000
I wake up every morning, with a few hours of sleep

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.460
with “Five Hundred Miles” stuck in my head.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.800
🎶When I wake up, will you know I’m gonna have this freaking song in my head🎶

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.600
I pack up, head out to the van that I still cannot believe exists,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.480
and then drive fife hundred miles or whatever,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.300
to the next place.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.580
The van is very comfortable, and we have neck pillows,

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.160
but it’s impossible to sleep in there,

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.920
Because one, it’s not a bed, and two,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.260
there is an Xbox, and so all we ever do is beat the holey living crap out of each other’s pixels.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.380
We arrive early afternoon

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.160
and find lots of books needing signatures and Hanklerfishes, which takes a couple hours.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.020
Although, fortunately, I have a fair bit of experience in the field of signing my name,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.060
and Hank, I’d wager that you've drawn more anglerfishes than anyone alive on the planet.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.280
And before you tell me that the plural of anglerfish is anglerfish,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.560
Wikipedia it!

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.560
Then the people start to show up and there are a lot of them.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.060
They wore my face on their torso, or Doctor Who shirts,

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.200
and they bring book cakes

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.620
and they have things I wrote tattooed on their bodies.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.300
Sometimes in borderline inappropriate places.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.220
All of which is amazing and beautiful

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.340
and also, of course, completely terrifying.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.860
Whispers: I’m nervous

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.480
Then we have a quick meeting with Hank Sock.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.900
Hank Sock: Hello, this is Hank Sock.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:12.680
Back stage, for the show. A little nervous, but uh,

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.400
a lot of people out there. I can see ‘em through the crack in the curtain.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.240
Back to Narration: And it’s time to start the show.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.360
Hank, writing is something you do alone. It’s a profession for introvers

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.940
who want to tell you a story but don’t want to make eye contact while telling it.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.680
And on some level, writing is the exact opposite

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.640
of this.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:37.660
*Croud screming in delight*

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.300
Then I read, and talk about The Fault in Our Stars,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.400
and you sing some songs,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.340
I answer some questions,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.300
you wear a tutu,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.420
we answered questions together and whoever is talking when the timer goes off

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:49.460
gets shocked with the Charlie is So CoolLike patented Shocker.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.360
*Hank gets shocked, crown cheers*

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.160
Then you sing some more songs, and people dance, and it feels magical

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.540
and otherworldly to be in a room full of people who feel unembarrassed

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.380
of their enthusiasm and intellect.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.700
🎶Hank sings🎶

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.520
And then we sign for five hours. Which I won’t show you much of

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.820
because the only thing more boring than standing in line,

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.020
is watching other people stand in line.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.600
Then we get to the hotel around 2 am, I sleep for a few hours

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.920
and wake up with “Five Hundred Miles” in my head, grateful

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.380
and astonished.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.180
To have the readers,

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.320
and the brother

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.400
I’ve lucked into.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.440
Hank, I’ll see you on Friday.

